OPPORTUNITY TEXT:
The World Meteorological Organization is accepting applications for a paid six-month internship in Geneva, Switzerland, within its Division of Development Partnerships and Programme Delivery.

The placement offers an exceptional entry point into the United Nations system for a Master’s-level candidate interested in international partnerships, philanthropy, private-sector engagement, sustainable finance, climate action, resource mobilization, due diligence, strategic communications and high-level event coordination.

The selected intern will join the Private Sector and Philanthropic Engagement Unit and work under the supervision of its Head. Rather than being limited to routine administrative support, the assignment covers partner research, meeting preparation, reputational-risk reviews, contributor engagement, briefing materials, knowledge management and support for major international platforms and events.

Applications must be submitted through the official WMO recruitment portal by 22 September 2026. The vacancy record is scheduled to close at 11:59 p.m. Geneva time. Candidates should apply early to avoid technical problems near the deadline. Full details are available on the official WMO vacancy page.

